    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for August 24th is anchored by **Nasim Nunez**, who leads the daily efficiency ratings with a 64.14 score. His matchup against Feltner is the primary driver, as the opposing starter\u2019s high 5.10 xERA provides a target-rich environment. While his projected #8 spot in the order is a slight drag on run-production potential, his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in the scarcest category (SB), making him an auto-start despite the lineup depth. **Sam Antonacci** also profiles as a high-upside play at 59.34; as a leadoff hitter facing Kumar Rocker, he benefits from a 10% efficiency bump for his position and a favorable platoon advantage that stabilizes his floor in a high-leverage slot.\n\nSecondary interest falls on **Miguel Vargas** (54.64) and **Tommy White** (55.05), both of whom are hovering in the marginal-to-strong range. **Tommy White** benefits from a +10% park factor which helps mitigate a neutral matchup against Zebby Matthews, while **Miguel Vargas** remains a viable UTIL start due to his recent xwOBA indicators. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** (49.04) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.55) are our most precarious starts. **Jackson Merrill** is battling a stiff test against Braxton Ashcraft\u2019s 3.28 xERA, dragging his efficiency score down despite the dynamic platoon advantage. We are currently navigating a \"Lineup Pending\" status for all active players; any last-minute defensive shifts or lineup slides from managers could jeopardize these efficiency scores, particularly for **Liam Hicks**, whose value is heavily tied to his projected #4 placement. As we look at the bench, **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are unavailable due to scheduled off-days, rendering our bench depth irrelevant for today\u2019s points accumulation. We must rely on our active core to provide the necessary SB volume from **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** to keep our Roto standing afloat while the stars rest.",
